  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>On the Plage de Gigaro, Marius à la Plage serves fresh Mediterranean cuisine in a lively atmosphere, enlivened by musical aperitifs — fresh produce and Mediterranean flavours praised in reviews, even though some find the prices high. Four-legged companions are welcome on the terrace, a detail specifically confirmed by one source, for a lunch or dinner almost with your feet in the sand.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>The on-site parking is a real plus, especially if you've come from hiking: it's the obvious stop after a walk on the Cap Lardier coastal path, which starts right nearby at Gigaro.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: pair the Gigaro → Cap Lardier hike with lunch here — the on-site parking saves you getting back in the car between the two.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The coastal path towards Cap Lardier starts very close by, one of the finest walks in the area with a dog.</p>
